## Part 6 — Verification

- **Typecheck is the fast loop.** Find the project's own script — read `package.json` (root and
  the app workspace) rather than guessing the command. With `strict`, `noUnusedLocals` and
  `noUnusedParameters` it catches most of what a linter would.
- **If a lint script fails on a missing dependency or a broken config rather than on the code,
  say so and move on.** A toolchain failure is not a finding.
- **Shadow-DOM components can't be typechecked into correctness.** Icon props, slot behaviour and
  radius overrides fail silently and only show on screen. Anything touching them needs a real
  browser check — hand that back to the human rather than claiming done.
- **Never spin up a mock API or browser automation to "verify" UI.** Typecheck, then the human's
  own browser.

